hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24008","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Muayqib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned wiping in the mosque, meaning the pebbles, and said: If you must do it, then once."
"24009","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Said, narrated to us Hisham, narrated to me Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, narrated to me Muayqib, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping in the mosque, meaning the pebbles, and he said: If you must do it, then once."
"24010","Narrated to us Khalaf ibn al-Walid, narrated to us Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Muayqib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"24011","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, narrated to me Muayqib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a man who levels the dust where he prostrates: He said: If you do it, then once."
